From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: tempeste <tempeste@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Wed, 11 Nov 2026 09:17:05 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 29/34] flashnext: TP=2 fidelity harness, relaxed and exact
 DeltaNet flags, prompt pieces beside rounds

A teacher-forced TP=2 fidelity harness (KL, top-1, draft acceptance), bf16 EXL3 prompt outputs, the riding
windows' front on the side stream, exact DeltaNet flags and an fp16 state option, deferred prompt pieces beside the
rounds (TF_FLASHNEXT_MIXED_BESIDE), pipelined RoCE chunks, round row logging, and pshare ride diagnostics.

Changes, in the order they were made:
- Add flashnext-fidelity-relax: teacher-forced TP=2 fidelity arms at 2k-200k contexts with KL, top-1, TV, MTP draft
  acceptance and a bootstrap gate against a noise floor
- Add TF_FLASHNEXT_Y_BF16: EXL3 prompt experts write y in bf16 and the slot sums read it (1: passes of 256+ rows, 2:
  every pass), with the flashnext-y-bf16 check and bench
- TF_FLASHNEXT_MIXED_RIDE_FRONT: the windows' front launches its glue kernels on the side stream too
- build: test-up126-host also runs the fill ranking's prefill-remaining tests (882ca0a77)
- DeltaNet: exact DeltaNet flags (compact q/k/v, norm in the state kernel, wide lanes) and a relaxed fp16 state
  product
- Add TF_FLASHNEXT_MIXED_BESIDE and the flashnext-mixed-beside bench
- RoCE one-shot: pipelined chunks behind TF_FLASHNEXT_TP_ROCE_PIPE_KB
- Serve TF_FLASHNEXT_MIXED_BESIDE: deferred prompt pieces beside the rounds
- flashnext-pshare-ride: probe the cause of cold fills parting, gate kept-state restores, compare turns under the same
  hook and company
- RIDE_FRONT: queue the windows' staged uploads on the side stream their kernels run on
- hcf wbdn: write back each row tile before its down instead of inside the previous tile's down
- Flash Next: TF_FLASHNEXT_ROUND_ROWS_PER_STREAM takes 5 and 6
- Lanes: TF_FLASHNEXT_ROWS_LOG, a shared round's rows and kept tokens
- tf-cuda-test: flashnext-rows and flashnext-rows-bench
- DeltaNet: TF_FLASHNEXT_GDN_STATE_F16, the DeltaNet state stored as fp16
- DeltaNet: TF_FLASHNEXT_GDN_WY_TRI, the WY block stored lower-triangular
- DeltaNet: drop two doc comments added with the fp16 state twins
- DeltaNet: the fp16 state twin choice is a runtime flag, only the field test is comptime
- gdn: under YS_BF16 a mark's short rest runs the one-block chain as the flag-off pass does
- gdn NORM_FUSED: load the chunk's gate values before the norm's barriers
- tf-cuda-test: install the segfault handler in every build mode
- flashnext-pshare-ride: tell float order from wrong state on a resumed turn
- flashnext-pshare-ride: gate same-mode comparisons byte-equal, report cross-mode ones against the tensor's RMS

Flags this patch adds (a flag's default is its unset value; unset leaves the engine as it was
before the flag, and a knob named under another flag only matters when that flag is on):
- TF_FLASHNEXT_GDN_CHUNK_RELAXED=1 (needs TF_FLASHNEXT_GDN_CHUNKED): the chunked DeltaNet chain's state products on
  fp16 mma, a relaxed (not byte-equal) path; off unset or 0.
- TF_FLASHNEXT_GDN_COMPACT=1 (needs TF_FLASHNEXT_GDN_YS_BF16): the chunked chain's q/k/v rows stored as bf16 with fp32
  scales, read back to the same fp32 bits; off unset or 0.
- TF_FLASHNEXT_GDN_LANES_WIDE=1: DeltaNet decode lanes in one table of up to 32 lanes (same bytes); off unset or 0.
- TF_FLASHNEXT_GDN_NORM_FUSED=1 (needs TF_FLASHNEXT_GDN_COMPACT): the gated norm runs inside the chunked state kernel,
  in the norm's own reduction order; off unset or 0.
- TF_FLASHNEXT_GDN_STATE_F16: added by the change "DeltaNet: TF_FLASHNEXT_GDN_STATE_F16, the DeltaNet state stored as
  fp16".
- TF_FLASHNEXT_GDN_WY_TRI: added by the change "DeltaNet: TF_FLASHNEXT_GDN_WY_TRI, the WY block stored
  lower-triangular".
- TF_FLASHNEXT_MIXED_BESIDE takes a deferred piece of at least its rows when none is beside and the prompt is not run
  whole
- TF_FLASHNEXT_MIXED_BESIDE_MIN is 1536 unset, takes 64 to the widest chunk's rows and refuses anything else
- TF_FLASHNEXT_ROWS_LOG is off unset or 0, on at 1, refuses anything else and leaves the identity alone
- TF_FLASHNEXT_TP_ROCE_PIPE_KB is off unset or 0, takes 64 to 1024 KiB in powers of two, refuses anything else, sets
  identity bits 47-49 alone and needs TF_FLASHNEXT_TP_ROCE at --tp 2
- TF_FLASHNEXT_Y_BF16: added by the change "Add TF_FLASHNEXT_Y_BF16: EXL3 prompt experts write y in bf16 and the slot
  sums read it (1: passes of 256+ rows, 2: every pass), with the flashnext-y-bf16 check and bench".
